    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us7000stbz](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us7000stbz) Magnitude 6.3 earthquake at 10.0 depth occurred on Jun 16 2026 260 km SSE of Dunhuang, China. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude 37.8888 longitude 95.4028. It impacted 1850 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
